{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration/recovery policy in specifications. The policy gives one dominant controllable per decision state, keeps all uncontrollable events defined in every spec state, treats obstacle events as safety-critical preemptions, uses brief backward escape only for front blockage, prefers short directed turns for side/front recovery, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion capability in G so E can impose safe one-shot action commitments.",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, use random_walk only as a secondary exploration mode, recover from obstacle_front via brief backward then directed turn, and allow full_rotate only from a dedicated stuck state after repeated blocked outcomes."
  ],
